  "details": "The angle that an avatar station is rotated affects whether VR tracking ends up lining up with the animation.\n\nSitting in an avatar station sometimes sends avatars peoples' view points in all directions when tracking returns. I've discovered that this is affected primarily on the angle the station object is upon entering a station. Y rotations are not affected while Z and X rotations consistently break when set at non zero angles. It seems the when tracking is restored the angles aren't applying properly.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n1. Create an avatar station at any angle X or Z\n\n2. Have another user in VR sit at the station\n\n3. Observe their new pretzel form\n\nThis has been reproducible using the avatar with ID:\n\navtr_8805f410-c141-4da1-848c-bd2d24e98226\n\nUnity package of this can be provided upon request.",
